paper-to-pipeline patch for GAPBS v1.5 (commit b5e3e19), applied by
scripts/build_gem5_workloads.sh with "patch -p1" in a fresh copy of the
source. It changes the benchmark harness in three ways, and none of them
touches a kernel function.

1. src/timer.h: the Timer never reads the clock. Under gem5 a clock read
   returns simulated time, so the printed timings would differ between the
   feature-on and feature-off runs, and so would the instructions that
   print them. GAPBS only prints timings. It never branches on them.

2. src/benchmark.h: a failed verification (-v) exits with status 1.
   Upstream prints FAIL and exits 0, and the gem5 run scripts read only
   the exit code.

3. src/benchmark.h: -v checks only the last trial, the same rule -a
   already follows. Measured under qemu on the scale-12 graph, one bfs
   trial costs 0.37 M instructions, and the check with -a adds about
   1.2 M. With a check on every trial, a many-trial run would mostly
   measure the serial checker, not the kernel.

   bfs, sssp and bc need one more line for this. Each verifier has its
   own SourcePicker, which picks the next source on every call. Called
   once, it would check the first source against the last trial's result
   and fail. SkipSources (src/benchmark.h) moves the verifier's picker past
   the unchecked trials, and src/bfs.cc, src/sssp.cc and src/bc.cc call
   it. Only main() changes in those files.

--- a/src/benchmark.h
+++ b/src/benchmark.h
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cinttypes>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <functional>
 #include <random>
 #include <utility>
@@ -68,6 +69,17 @@
 };
 
 
+// paper-to-pipeline: BenchmarkKernel checks only the last trial, but a
+// verifier's SourcePicker picks one source per call, starting from the
+// first. Skipping the sources of the unchecked trials makes the verifier
+// check the source that the last trial used.
+template<typename GraphT_>
+void SkipSources(SourcePicker<GraphT_> &sp, int64_t count) {
+  for (int64_t i = 0; i < count; i++)
+    sp.PickNext();
+}
